  "purpose": "Editorial rehabilitation overlay for the saved BBC Good Food corpus. It preserves each source card and generates a measured, locally executable Mise baseline without mutating the imported source dataset.",
  "methodology": {
    "sourceEvidence": "Amounts, yield, timing and component references are taken from the stored Good Food candidate cards. Optional serving suggestions are deliberately outside a plated production baseline unless a card explicitly supplies a measured amount.",
    "measurementPolicy": "Ambiguous household descriptions use the documented average-mass ledger in the apply script; the generated ingredient keeps the original wording in provenance.",
    "nutritionPolicy": "The apply script retains publisher nutrition in sourceNutrition and derives Mise macros from the complete measured baseline. It never relabels publisher figures as independently verified.",
    "procedurePolicy": "Existing Russian paraphrases are retained only after every referenced component has been replaced by a measured local equivalent. No publisher procedure text is copied."
  },
